  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_030 (multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) scored 0.632, which is notably below the RNA-only scvi_n200 baselines (config_005: 0.650, config_006: 0.653), suggesting that naive concat fusion of a weak image modality (image-only resnet50: 0.208) actively hurts performance. Question: Does weighted fusion, which can down-weight the weaker image branch, recover the RNA-only performance or even exceed it? config_031 is identical to config_030 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating fusion as the sole variable. Why this is the best next step: It is the cleanest single-variable comparison available to determine whether resnet50 image carries any salvageable signal in a multimodal setting. If weighted fusion still underperforms RNA-only, we can confidently deprioritize resnet50-based multimodal configs and redirect budget toward RNA-only refinement or a stronger image encoder (ViT-L). If it recovers to ~0.65+, it justifies further multimodal exploration with resnet50. This single experiment resolves a critical fork in the search strategy under limited budget."
}

